        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "174ee08d-e56a-5f60-b070-8b5c2cd41fd8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Spot Marks the X; Alice in Wonderland (1985 film)\n- People: Mike the Dog; Barret Oliver; Natalie Gregory; Lewis Carroll\n- Organizations: Disney Channel; CBS\n- Roles: Capone/Astro; Ken; Kathy\n- Topics: television film adaptations; broadcast dates; cast credits\n\nFacts:\n- Alice in Wonderland is a 1985 two-part made-for-television film adaptation of Lewis Carroll's books Alice's Adventures in Wonderland and Through the Looking-Glass.\n- Alice in Wonderland first aired on CBS on December 9, 1985 for part one and on December 10, 1985 for part two, both at 8:00 pm EST.\n- Spot Marks the X is a 1986 Disney Channel Original Movie.\n- Spot Marks the X starred Mike the Dog as Capone/Astro, Barret Oliver as Ken, and Natalie Gregory as Kathy.\n- Mike the Dog was known from Down and Out in Beverly Hills before appearing in Spot Marks the X.\n- Barret Oliver was known from The Neverending Story, Frankenweenie, D.A.R.Y.L., and Cocoon before appearing in Spot Marks the X.\n- Natalie Gregory was known from Alice in Wonderland, Oliver & Company, and Cranium Command before appearing in Spot Marks the X.\n- In Spot Marks the X, Natalie Gregory's character Kathy is shown with Natalie Gregory's real brunette hair, unlike her appearance as Alice in the 1985 Alice in Wonderland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3809444f-0dd2-5096-98a9-91686c47951f",
        "text": "Page: Spot Marks the X. Sentence: Spot Marks the X is a 1986 Disney Channel Original Movie that starred Mike the Dog (from \"Down and Out in Beverly Hills\") as Capone/Astro, Barret Oliver (from \"The Neverending Story\", \"Frankenweenie\", \"D.A.R.Y.L\", and \"Cocoon\") as Ken, and Natalie Gregory (from \"Alice in Wonderland (1985 version)\", \"Oliver & Company\", and \"Cranium Command\") as Kathy, who, unlike her role as Alice in the aforementioned 1985 version, is seen with her real hair in this movie, which is brunette.\nPage: Alice in Wonderland (1985 film). Sentence: Alice in Wonderland is a 1985 two-part made-for-television film adaptation of Lewis Carroll's books \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland\" and \"Through the Looking-Glass\".\nPage: Alice in Wonderland (1985 film). Sentence: \"Alice in Wonderland\" was first telecast December 9, 1985, (part one) and December 10, 1985 (part two), at 8:00pm EST on CBS.",
